## Prevention of Neurodegenerative Diseases

The report of the *Lancet* standing Commission on dementia prevention lists among the modifiable risk factors, among others, physical inactivity, high blood pressure, depression, social isolation and hearing loss ([Livingston et al., 2024](https://doi.org/10.1016/S0140-6736(24)01296-0), *Lancet*); this is a summary of observational data. A spa stay offers an environment where several of these factors can be worked on at once:

- Regular exercise under the guidance of a physiotherapist
- Regular sleep in a quiet environment
- Company — shared treatments, concerts on the colonnade, walks in a group
- Less stress
- A blood pressure check at the initial examination and an exercise regimen you take home with you

A preventive stay is not covered by health insurance; you come as a self-paying guest. Prevention is the investment that pays off most of all. More about [preventive care at the spa](/en/magazine/prevention-new-luxury-spa).

## When a Stay Is Not Suitable

Diseases in the acute stage and conditions at risk of destabilisation are among the general [contraindications to spa care](/en/indications-and-contraindications). For neurological diagnoses, the suitability of spa treatment is decided by the treating neurologist and then by the spa physician at the initial examination.
